{"id": "EUVD-2026-86182", "enisaUuid": "315f97d0-df50-3588-8548-0f87ac1a8577", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblk-cgroup: fix leaks and online flag on radix_tree_insert failure\n\nWhen radix_tree_insert() fails in blkg_create(), the error path has two\nissues:\n\n1. blkg->online is set to true unconditionally, even when the blkg was\n   never fully inserted.  Move the assignment inside the success block.\n\n2. The error path calls blkg_put() without first calling\n   percpu_ref_kill().  Because the refcount is still in percpu mode,\n   percpu_ref_put() only does this_cpu_sub() without checking for zero,\n   so blkg_release() is never triggered.  This permanently leaks the\n   blkg memory, its percpu iostat, policy data, the parent blkg\n   reference, and the cgroup css reference \u2014 the latter preventing the\n   cgroup from ever being destroyed.\n\nFix by replacing blkg_put() with percpu_ref_kill(), matching the pattern\nused in blkg_destroy().", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f840db042caee9d2f3dcdcf97d6674f6e4c1e30", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f53945d7c712efe63fadbcc5ffed6370871fd0d3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ada8270ccdb6f212da5eb22614c28ea418746a4a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3650be82ef6e7af13b79b2d10a7363bdf54aa7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e85f02d45b5977c0326a8d854c6db878aa6b34a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c0d150fb98ea40760611979f4e664c244b20966", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbbca20764382b4d411ec2918f4e278ffe547acc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q3xm-frv6-mwqx", "CVE-2026-93795"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "157c01c0-86db-312a-a6b5-1808f976b2f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fcf2b033b84e261dca283bc2911aaea4b07b525 <dbbca20764382b4d411ec2918f4e278ffe547acc"}, {"id": "30804103-420a-39ea-9397-89c4baa4a527", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fcf2b033b84e261dca283bc2911aaea4b07b525 <c3650be82ef6e7af13b79b2d10a7363bdf54aa7f"}, {"id": "3222b320-9460-33a0-ae03-16b2cfda878c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "46678e0e-2916-3921-ba97-050a5e14f0b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fcf2b033b84e261dca283bc2911aaea4b07b525 <f53945d7c712efe63fadbcc5ffed6370871fd0d3"}, {"id": "6b7358fc-f5c0-3d82-9ffd-f4396872d712", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "793f41be-fbc5-34e5-a1ff-19ac7976cbe2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fcf2b033b84e261dca283bc2911aaea4b07b525 <0f840db042caee9d2f3dcdcf97d6674f6e4c1e30"}, {"id": "895a5670-773a-3b4e-9dcf-b554af42b436", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "98bb71a9-aadb-346c-9a90-9eb65c2e0576", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "9a2cfd77-6577-3973-8e1d-5d7fd1c5af10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "a6523c8f-9baf-3fbd-a5b1-dfb2459798c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7fcf2b033b84e261dca283bc2911aaea4b07b525 <4c0d150fb98ea40760611979f4e664c244b20966"}, {"id": "a93d0638-c0ed-3a0e-b986-925c9bfedc90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "b96d6632-05d2-3fd5-b99c-1adbae8bcb6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "bb76f05c-0ddb-3f97-8abe-225816562b99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "d8db93e2-a9b5-398a-b9c2-6fb